### C25D 1.0 test pattern: parallel_plate
### Purpose: closed-form capacitance validation for C25D_parser.py.
### Single top plate over an infinite ground plane, uniform background
### dielectric (no SIMPLE/SIDEWALL/CONFORMAL layers), so there is no
### epsilon-resolution ambiguity in this first test, only GROUND_PLANE, METAL,
### DIELECTRIC_BACKGROUND, CONDUCTOR, BOX, and DOMAIN_MARGIN.
###
### Geometry (chosen for a clean closed-form comparison):
###   plate area A = 50um x 50um = 2500 um^2
###   separation  d = 2um (ground plane top at z=0, plate bottom at z=2.0)
###   background permittivity epsr = 4.0
###   closed-form target: C = eps0 * epsr * A / d = 44.2709 fF

C25D 1.0
UNITS LENGTH um

META technology test_synthetic
META source_cell parallel_plate

#---------------- GROUND PLANE ----------------
# Infinite XY conductor at 0V, occupies -0.100 <= z <= 0.000.
GROUND_PLANE SUB Z_OFFSETS -0.100 0.000

#---------------- LAYER (metal) ----------------
# Top plate sits on this layer. 2.000um gap from ground plane top (z=0)
# to layer bottom (z=2.000) gives the separation d used in the closed-form
# target above.
METAL M1 Z_OFFSETS 2.000 2.050

#---------------- DIELECTRICS ----------------
# No DIELECTRIC_SIMPLE/SIDEWALL/CONFORMAL layers - background alone fills
# all volume not occupied by the ground plane or the plate conductor,
# so the entire gap between plates is uniformly epsr = 4.0.
DIELECTRIC_BACKGROUND diel PERMITTIVITY 4.000

#---------------- NETS and SHAPES ----------------
# Single conductor: PLATE. Capacitance matrix will report its
# self-capacitance to the (implicit 0V) ground plane.
CONDUCTOR PLATE PLATE.net

# 50um x 50um square, centered at origin.
BOX CONDUCTOR PLATE LAYER M1 LL -25.000 -25.000 UR 25.000 25.000

#---------------- DOMAIN ----------------
# Generous margin relative to plate size/separation so the finite
# computational boundary doesn't perturb the near-field result.
DOMAIN_MARGIN X 20.000 Y 20.000 Z 20.000
